HEAD is now at 05f6b0f no-mistakes(ci): Fixed ci-2 (Greptile P1): a pushed GitLab task with a merged merge request could not be torn down when later default-branch changes made the content check conflict. Invariant: `pr_is_merged` must read a recorded PR through the reader for its own forge. Before the fix, every address that was not Forgejo went to `gh pr view`, which cannot read GitLab or Gerrit addresses. Changes: - `bin/fm-pr-lib.sh`: `fm_pr_gitlab_read_record` now also sets `FM_PR_RECORD_HEAD` from the MR record's `sha` field (empty when missing), so existing callers accept the same records as before. - `bin/fm-teardown.sh` `pr_is_merged`: one `case` on the provider. forgejo uses `fm_pr_forgejo_read_record` (unchanged). gitlab uses `fm_pr_gitlab_read_record`. gerrit uses `fm_pr_gerrit_read_record` plus `fm_pr_gerrit_read_revision`. github and branch-resolved PR numbers still use `gh pr view`. For the provider readers, the merged state must be `true` and the head must pass `fm_pr_head_valid`. The containment proof is unchanged: `ensure_commit_object`, then HEAD is an ancestor of the merged head, or the unpushed patch-ids are in the PR head. - `tests/fm-teardown.test.sh`: new test `test_pushed_gitlab_task_with_merged_mr_allows_when_main_moved_on`, with a stubbed glab. MR merged: teardown proceeds. MR opened: teardown proceeds. MR closed without merging: teardown refuses and keeps the task state. Verification: - The new test fails without the bin changes ("REFUSED ... work that is not landed") and passes with them. - `tests/fm-teardown.test.sh` and `tests/fm-crew-state.test.sh` exited 0 with no failures. - The background test run was stopped at its time limit before it printed final exit codes for `fm-pr-merge`, `fm-project-mode` and `fm-pr-check-security`. Their logs show no failures: fm-pr-merge 123 passed, fm-project-mode 12 passed ("all assertions passed"), fm-pr-check-security 37 passed. - `bin/fm-lint.sh` on the three changed files is clean. - Not tested against a real GitLab server; the tests use a stub glab
